php-geos (1.2.0+git20260426-1~jammy1) jammy; urgency=medium

  * GEOSSTRtree::nearest gains optional second argument
    nearest(GEOSGeometry $g, ?int $k = null) :
      - $k === null  -> scalar single-nearest payload (or null on empty tree),
                        unchanged from 1.1.x.
      - $k >= 1      -> array of up to $k payloads sorted nearest-first.
      - $k <= 0      -> throws.
    Implemented as a max-heap-of-k traversal via GEOSSTRtree_iterate_r:
    O(n log k) time, O(k) space, public-API only. Not index-aware
    pruning (libgeos's STRtree internals are not exposed by the public
    C API), but fast enough for typical workloads (n in thousands,
    k single-digit) and strictly faster than the PHP-side
    bbox-expand+sort fallback. If/when libgeos exposes a true
    k-nearest API, swap for a direct call.

  * GEOSSTRtree::query and ::iterate callbacks gain early-termination:
    a strict boolean false return signals "stop calling me". GEOS's
    internal C-side traversal still completes (no public way to abort
    mid-iteration), but the user's callback is not invoked for
    subsequent items. Returning null/void or true continues iteration
    as before — strict false is the only sentinel.

  * Tests: 9 new sub-cases in 030_STRtree.phpt covering k-NN happy
    paths, k>n cap, empty-tree, $k <= 0 throws, plus iterate / query
    early-termination + the negative case (true/null does not stop).

 -- Abraham van der Merwe <abz@frogfoot.com>  Sun, 26 Apr 2026 21:00:00 +0200

php-geos (1.1.2+git20260426-1~jammy1) jammy; urgency=medium

  * Fix segfault in GEOSSTRtree::remove() when called after the tree
    has been queried/iterated/nearest'd. libgeos's STRtree is bulk-loaded;
    once internal construction triggers, mutation hits undefined behaviour.
    The build-once gate that already protected insert() now also covers
    remove(); a clean exception is raised instead of crashing.
  * Fix latent dangling-reference hazard in GEOSSTRtree::insert(): the
    tree previously stored the caller's GEOSGeometry* envelope pointer
    directly. Dropping the caller's $env zval before the first query
    could leave a stale reference inside the C tree. The binding now
    stores its own cloned envelope (box->env) and uses it consistently
    in both insert() and remove(), so caller-side env lifetime no
    longer matters after insert returns.
  * Two regression tests added in 030_STRtree.phpt:
    testRemoveAfterNearestRejected, testInsertEnvLifetimeAfterCallerDrops.

 -- Abraham van der Merwe <abz@frogfoot.com>  Sun, 26 Apr 2026 20:00:00 +0200

php-geos (1.1.1+git20260426-1~jammy1) jammy; urgency=medium

  * Fix getZvalAsDouble silently truncating fractional floats to integers.
    The function was declared to return long despite reading Z_DVAL; the
    truncation was masked because all callers assigned the result to
    double targets. Affected call sites: GEOSCoordSeq::copyFromArrays
    (reported in the field), buffer style 'mitre_limit', and
    coverageClean params 'snap_distance' / 'gap_max_width'.
  * Add regression test
    006_CoordSeq.phpt::testCopyFromArraysPreservesFractionalFloats.

 -- Abraham van der Merwe <abz@frogfoot.com>  Sun, 26 Apr 2026 19:00:00 +0200

php-geos (1.1.0+git20260426-1~jammy1) jammy; urgency=medium

  * Major upstream extension: fork at github.com/avdmerwe/php-geos targeting
    libgeos 3.14.x. Minimum required GEOS bumped to 3.11.0; all
    HAVE_GEOS_* feature-detection gates dropped from config.m4, geos.c,
    arginfo.h.
  * New class GEOSCoordSeq (Item 2): foundational sequence type with
    full Z/M support, copyFromArrays/copyToArrays, lifecycle hand-off
    semantics for use as a constructor argument.
  * New methods on GEOSGeometry:
    - MakeValid family with linework + structure modes (Item 3).
    - Concave hulls: concaveHull, concaveHullByLength,
      concaveHullOfPolygons, polygonHullSimplify (Item 4).
    - Precision-grid overlays: optional gridSize on intersection,
      difference, symDifference, union (Item 5).
    - WKB flavor toggle (EXTENDED / ISO) and fix-structure on
      WKT/WKB readers (Item 7).
    - Hull and metric extras: minimumBoundingCircle,
      minimumRotatedRectangle, minimumWidth, minimumClearance,
      minimumClearanceLine, maximumInscribedCircle, largestEmptyCircle
      (Item 8).
    - Distance extras: distanceWithin, distanceIndexed, nearestPoints,
      frechetDistance(+Densify), hausdorffDistanceDensify (Item 9).
    - Linear-referencing extras: lineSubstring, lineMergeDirected
      (Item 10).
    - Construction utilities: reverse, densify, removeRepeatedPoints,
      orientPolygons, equalsIdentical, getX/Y min/max, getExtent,
      buildArea, plus standalone GEOSPolygonizeValid,
      GEOSPolygonizeCutEdges, GEOSBuildArea, GEOSDisjointSubsetUnion
      (Item 11).
    - Curved-geometry constructors: createCircularString,
      createCompoundCurve, createCurvePolygon, plus type-id constants
      (Item 12).
    - Coverage processing: coverageUnion, coverageIsValid,
      coverageSimplifyVW, coverageClean (Item 13).
    - Clustering: clusterDBSCAN, clusterByDistance,
      clusterByIntersection returning new GEOSClusterResult (Item 14).
    - Constrained Delaunay via $constrained option (Item 15).
    - Geometry construction factories: createPoint(+FromXY+Empty),
      createLineString, createLinearRing, createPolygon,
      createCollection, createRectangle (Item 16).
    - Coordinate-transform callbacks: transformXY, transformXYZ
      (Item 19).
    - P2 fillers: hilbertCode, gridIntersectionFractions,
      orientationIndex, segmentIntersection (Item 20).
  * New classes:
    - GEOSGeoJSONReader / GEOSGeoJSONWriter (Item 6).
    - GEOSClusterResult (Item 14).
    - GEOSSTRtree spatial index with callback iteration, payload
      box-allocation, sticky-error exception propagation (Item 17).
    - GEOSPreparedGeometry with full predicate set, distance, and
      nearestPoints (Item 18).
  * Backwards compatible with 1.0.0 callers; no removed or renamed
    methods.
  * 25 .phpt test files (000-005 baseline + 006-060 feature suites),
    all green against libgeos 3.14.1.

 -- Abraham van der Merwe <abz@frogfoot.com>  Sun, 26 Apr 2026 17:30:00 +0200

php-geos (1.0.0+git20240129-2~jammy1) jammy; urgency=medium

  * Update tests/*.phpt assertions for libgeos 3.14.1 default behavioural
    changes. Six tests (000-005) were previously passing 5/6 against
    libgeos 3.10.2 but failing 4/6 against 3.14.1; they now pass 6/6:
    - 001 Geometry: WKT writer canonicalises -0 -> 0; empty intersection
      returns input-type EMPTY (POINT EMPTY rather than GEOMETRYCOLLECTION
      EMPTY for POINT-POINT etc); polygon ring start vertex normalised to
      lex-smallest; collection member ordering changed; mitre-join
      buffer corner clamping shifted; offsetCurve right-side reversed
      orientation + denser interpolation; MULTIPOINT WKT format now
      `MULTIPOINT ((x y), ...)`; argument-type exception messages broadened
      ("Polygon" -> "Surface", "LineString" -> "Curve" / "SimpleCurve").
      Fixed three pre-existing WKT parse-typo testcases that 3.10's lenient
      parser silently accepted (extra `)` in GEOMETRYCOLLECTION literals).
    - 002 WKTWriter: default trim is now TRUE; setRoundingPrecision(0)
      yields trimmed output; setOutputDimension accepts 4 (XYZM); error
      message text broadened to "must be 2, 3, or 4".
    - 004 WKBWriter: getOutputDimension default is now 4 (XYZM); accepts
      4 as valid; error message broadened.
    - 005 WKBReader: round-trip WKT data updated for new MULTIPOINT format.

